notes.content:
Import scheme: flat. Run: python main.py. Smoke: echo "quit" | python main.py. Files: models.py, loader.py, parser.py, engine.py, main.py.
Data shapes:
  world.yaml → loader.py: Top-level mapping with 5 required keys: rooms (dict of room ID to room data), items (dict of item ID to item data), npcs (dict of NPC ID to NPC data), monsters (dict of monster ID to monster data), start_room (str). Each room has name (str), description (str), connections (dict of direction to room ID), items (list of item IDs), npcs (list of NPC IDs), monsters (list of monster IDs). Each item has name (str), type (str: weapon/armor/healing/key), stats (dict of stat modifiers), description (str). Each NPC has name (str), dialogue (list of str), quest_flags (list of str). Each monster has name (str), health (int), attack (int), behavior (str: aggressive/passive/guard), loot (list of item IDs), optional phases (list of phase dicts for boss).
State contracts:
  Player state (owner engine.py, consumers engine.py, parser.py, main.py): location: str, health: int, max_health: int, base_attack: int, inventory: list[str] (item IDs), equipment: {weapon: str | None, armor: str | None}, flags: dict[str, bool]
  Room state (owner engine.py, consumers engine.py): visited: bool, items: list[str] (item IDs present), npcs: list[str] (NPC IDs present), monster: str | None (monster ID if present), looted: bool
  NPC state (owner engine.py, consumers engine.py): dialogue_stage: int, quest_flags: list[str]
  Persisted save JSON (owner engine.py, consumers engine.py): {player: {location: str, health: int, max_health: int, base_attack: int, inventory: list[str], equipment: {weapon: str | None, armor: str | None}, flags: dict[str, bool]}, current_room_id: str, room_states: dict[str, {visited: bool, items: list[str], npcs: list[str], monster: str | None, looted: bool}], npc_states: dict[str, {dialogue_stage: int, quest_flags: list[str]}], defeated_monsters: list[str], playtime_seconds: float}
  load_world() return / GameEngine.__init__ input (owner loader.py, consumers engine.py, main.py): {rooms: dict[str, Room], items: dict[str, Item], npcs: dict[str, NPC], monsters: dict[str, Monster], start_room: str}
  parse_command() return / GameEngine.execute_command input (owner parser.py, consumers engine.py): {type: CommandType, target: str | None, args: dict[str, str | None]}
